{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791301308,"nonce":"ui/BRCFebu8NRtvMVfmcVT3TbgM=","title":"LLVM: run select optimization for floating-point loop recurrences on x86","message":"The default x86 machine pipeline runs the integer cmov converter but omits the IR select-optimize pass. HIR loop specialization (59a95c56d47bf4b172fc81f71e7b6f2db5b234897e8be577d8071fd2f8e62703) exposes a float-only recurrence in Lua Collatz; SimplifyCFG turns its branch into a select, extending the critical path. NUC checksum-verified medians regress from 155 ms to 291 ms despite successful OSR and only about 2 ms extra LLVM compilation. Lowering phi folding thresholds restores about 130 ms but affects unrelated branch transformations.\n\nRunning LLVM 21 select-optimize on captured post-O3 IR with the host target recognizes the recurrence as profitable to branch (estimated branch cost 31 versus select cost 54). Test adding this standard cost-based pass after O2/O3 on x86 and setting host function attributes before optimization. Keep normal interpreter-first tiering and verify every benchmark checksum.","files":null}]}